Z||000007||Philphine||08-31-2001||04:25 PM||||were you the one going into the af? remember what i said. don't try to impress them by doing more or try to get away with doing less. a lot of basic is seeing how well you take/follow orders. study the training manual when you can (you'll have time. don't waste it) and the test will be easy. it's not fun at all but it's really not hard. the goal is to make it last only as long as it has to.<P>i saw a couple of people get washed back for little reasons like talking in formation. there was one guy who just wouldn't shut up (just think what do you really need to say at that moment that's worth getting in trouble for). also a guy who forgot to sign back in when we got a town pass. they knew he was there but since he missed that detail they washed him back.<P>hope im not scaring you. it really is just a matter of following orders. i'm a pinhead and i came out as a honor grad. <P>good luck.<P>uh...if you weren't the one going to basic let me quote emily littela and say...<P>"nevermind"   ||||reg||1
